{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs22 Use-Case Flow Specification - Lab 1\line Use Case: Run Daily Audit (WHOIS & SSL Check)\line\line Primary Actor(s): SysAdmin\line Supporting Actor(s): WHOIS Service, Notification Service\line Goal: Obtain current domain/certificate expiry status and issue alerts before expiration.\line\line PRECONDITIONS\line1. The monitoring engine is configured with at least one monitored domain/SSL endpoint and a valid daily schedule.\line2. The system can reach monitored endpoints and the WHOIS service.\line\line POSTCONDITIONS\line1. WHOIS and SSL/TLS audit results are updated.\line2. Required alerts are generated and passed to the configured escalation path.\line3. Audit results and alert activity are stored for later review.\line\line MAIN SUCCESS SCENARIO\line1. The scheduler triggers the daily audit.\line2. The system retrieves the monitored domains and SSL endpoints.\line3. For each domain, the system performs a WHOIS lookup to obtain registration and expiration information.\line4. For each SSL endpoint, the system performs a TLS handshake and extracts the certificate expiration date.\line5. The system compares expiry dates with the current date.\line6. If an expiry is within 30, 15, or 3 days, the system creates the corresponding alert.\line7. The system stores audit results and generated alerts.\line8. The system sends alerts through the configured escalation ladder.\line9. The audit completes and the dashboard reflects the latest status.\line\line ALTERNATE FLOW A - EXTERNAL SERVICE UNAVAILABLE\lineA1. WHOIS service or a monitored SSL endpoint is unreachable or times out.\lineA2. The system retries using the configured retry/timeout policy.\lineA3. If the retry fails, the system records the item as failed and continues with remaining endpoints.\lineA4. The failure is recorded for review and, where configured, the SysAdmin is notified.\line\line ALTERNATE FLOW B - ALERT ACKNOWLEDGED\lineB1. A recipient acknowledges the alert.\lineB2. The system records the acknowledgement and stops further escalation for that alert.\line}